title: TrialEmulation (Python)
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vermeulen
    given-names: Xander
    email: Xander.Vermeulen@mwdh.co.uk
  - family-names: Sainsbury
    given-names: Chris
    email: chris.sainsbury@mwdh.co.uk
repository-code: "https://github.com/csainsbury/Trial-Emulation-R2P"
url: "https://trial-emulation.readthedocs.io"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.5.1
date-released: 2026-09-17
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - trial emulation
  - marginal structural models
  - epidemiology
  - observational studies
  - target trial
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of target trial emulation methods for causal
  inference in observational time-to-event data. This package provides
  tools to emulate a sequence of randomized trials from longitudinal
  observational data and estimate treatment effects using marginal
  structural models with inverse probability weighting.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "TrialEmulation: Causal Analysis of Observational Time-to-Event Data"
    authors:
      - name: "Causal-LDA Team"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Causal-LDA/TrialEmulation"
    notes: "Original R package implementation"
